# Maximized (WindowFill): with the sidebar docked the card keeps its 10 pt inset and rounded corners;
# hidden, the card goes edge to edge with the window's own zoom animation, and restoring brings the
# inset back as the window shrinks (ShellView.beginZoom). Both the zoom command (the green button
# with ⌥, Window ▸ Zoom) and a title strip double-click (with the system set to Maximize) do it.
cra://debug?windowSize=1000x700
wait 2
cra://debug?zoomWindow=1
wait 1.5
cra://debug?windowState=maxDocked
expect-log window state maxDocked: main0 .*card=328,10,.* docked=1
cra://debug?zoomWindow=1
wait 1.5
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 1
cra://debug?titleDoubleClick=Maximize
wait 1.5
cra://debug?windowState=maxHidden
expect-log window state maxHidden: main0 .*card=0,0,.* docked=0
cra://debug?titleDoubleClick=Maximize
wait 1.5
cra://debug?windowState=restored
expect-log window state restored: main0 .*size=1000x700 card=10,10,980,680 docked=0
